# The plain-English work log. Every loop-built PR prepends one dated entry to
# the top of this file, so any two branches open at the same time collide here
# even though neither touched the other's entry — and both entries are always
# keepers. On 2026-08-22 a single merge turned 17 of 23 open PRs from clean to
# conflicting on this file alone, one after another, because each merge
# re-conflicts every branch still waiting.
#
# `union` is git's BUILT-IN driver: on a conflicting hunk it keeps both sides'
# lines instead of writing markers. That is exactly right for a prepend-only
# log — both new entries land at the top, newest-first order is preserved, and
# nothing is dropped. Verified before adding this line: merging main into the
# `main-guard` branch went from one conflicted file to zero, with every heading
# from BOTH sides present in the result.
#
# This needs no registration in .git/config and no install step, because git
# ships it. (Unlike the retired `asset-pins` driver that used to live in this
# file — removed 2026-08-24, task 86bbkh288, when committed HTML stopped
# carrying ?v= pins and there was nothing left for it to merge.) GitHub
# honours it server-side, so "Update branch" on a pull request stops conflicting.
#
# A genuine edit to the SAME entry by two branches would still be merged by
# keeping both lines rather than flagging it — acceptable here, because entries
# are append-only history that nobody goes back and rewrites.
docs/WORK-LOG.md merge=union
